@startuml
title Where the plaintext lives in five confidential systems
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam componentBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam componentBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #FAFCFF
skinparam packageBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F5F9FF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

package "Per-owner notes, read locally" {
  component "Zcash\nnote commitments,\nshielded pool,\npayments only" as ZC
  component "Railgun\nnote commitments\nin an EVM contract,\ntoken transfers" as RG
  component "Aztec\nnote commitments\n+ public data tree,\narbitrary contracts" as AZ
}

package "Ciphertext computed on in place" {
  component "Zama FHE\none network key,\ncoprocessor evaluates,\nKMS committee decrypts" as ZM
}

package "Plaintext held by the entitled parties" {
  component "Canton\nsub-transaction views,\neach validator stores\nonly its parties' data" as CN
}

note bottom of AZ
  The owner holds the viewing and
  nullifier keys, decrypts locally,
  and proves the transition. No third
  party is asked for permission.
end note

note bottom of ZM
  Nobody holds the full key. Reading
  your own value needs a live, authorised
  round trip to the threshold committee.
end note

note bottom of CN
  No global replicated state at all.
  Confidentiality comes from not sending
  the data, not from encrypting it.
end note
@enduml
